    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "It can easily highlight hex colors by using `MiniHipatterns.gen_highlighter.hex_color`.\r\nBut I often use colors in HSL.\r\nCould you tell me how to make one for hsl?\r\nMy current config looks like so:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n    local hi = require(\"mini.hipatterns\")\r\n\r\n    local hsl_pattern = \"hsl.()%d+(), ()%d+(), ()%d+()\"\r\n\r\n    return {\r\n      highlighters = {\r\n        hex_color = hi.gen_highlighter.hex_color({ priority = 2000 }),\r\n        hsl_color = {\r\n          pattern = function()\r\n            return hsl_pattern\r\n          end,\r\n          group = function(_, _, data)\r\n            print(vim.inspect(data))\r\n            return MiniHipatterns.compute_hex_color_group(data.full_match, \"full\")\r\n          end,\r\n          priority = 2000,\r\n        },\r\n      },\r\n```\r\n\r\nAny help would be appreciated!",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">It can easily highlight hex colors by using <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniHipatterns.gen_highlighter.hex_color</code>.<br>\nBut I often use colors in HSL.<br>\nCould you tell me how to make one for hsl?<br>\nMy current config looks like so:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    local hi = require(&quot;mini.hipatterns&quot;)\n\n    local hsl_pattern = &quot;hsl.()%d+(), ()%d+(), ()%d+()&quot;\n\n    return {\n      highlighters = {\n        hex_color = hi.gen_highlighter.hex_color({ priority = 2000 }),\n        hsl_color = {\n          pattern = function()\n            return hsl_pattern\n          end,\n          group = function(_, _, data)\n            print(vim.inspect(data))\n            return MiniHipatterns.compute_hex_color_group(data.full_match, &quot;full&quot;)\n          end,\n          priority = 2000,\n        },\n      },\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">hi</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.hipatterns<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">hsl_pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>hsl.()%d+(), ()%d+(), ()%d+()<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">highlighters</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">hex_color</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">hi</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_highlighter</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">hex_color</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">priority</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">2000</span> }),\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">hsl_color</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n          <span class=\"pl-en\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n            <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">hsl_pattern</span>\n          <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n          <span class=\"pl-en\">group</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">_</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">_</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">data</span>)\n            <span class=\"pl-c1\">print</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">inspect</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">data</span>))\n            <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniHipatterns</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">compute_hex_color_group</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">data</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">full_match</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>full<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n          <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n          <span class=\"pl-smi\">priority</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">2000</span>,\n        },\n      },</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Any help would be appreciated!</p>",
    "bodyText": "It can easily highlight hex colors by using MiniHipatterns.gen_highlighter.hex_color.\nBut I often use colors in HSL.\nCould you tell me how to make one for hsl?\nMy current config looks like so:\n    local hi = require(\"mini.hipatterns\")\n\n    local hsl_pattern = \"hsl.()%d+(), ()%d+(), ()%d+()\"\n\n    return {\n      highlighters = {\n        hex_color = hi.gen_highlighter.hex_color({ priority = 2000 }),\n        hsl_color = {\n          pattern = function()\n            return hsl_pattern\n          end,\n          group = function(_, _, data)\n            print(vim.inspect(data))\n            return MiniHipatterns.compute_hex_color_group(data.full_match, \"full\")\n          end,\n          priority = 2000,\n        },\n      },\nAny help would be appreciated!",
