            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Basically, this boils down to programming two parts:\r\n- [Pattern to be highlighted](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1fdbb864e2015eb6f501394d593630f825154385/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L149-L161).\r\n- [Group used to highlight pattern matches](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1fdbb864e2015eb6f501394d593630f825154385/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L163-L174). \r\n\r\nIn case of HSL the real problem is to convert matched color representation in HSL to its hex string (which is the only big color space Neovim highlight groups support).\r\n\r\nHere is an example of how I would do it to highlight one of the CSS formats like `hsl(50 80% 40%)` (taken from [here](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/hsl)):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal hsl_to_hex = function(h, s, l)\r\n  -- Actually convert h, s, l numbers into hex color in '#RRGGBB' format\r\n  return '#111111'\r\nend\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.hipatterns').setup({\r\n  highlighters = {\r\n    hsl_color = {\r\n      pattern = 'hsl%(%d+ %d+%% %d+%%%)',\r\n      group = function(_, match)\r\n        local h, s, l = match:match('hsl%((%d+) (%d+)%% (%d+)%%%)')\r\n        h, s, l = tonumber(h), tonumber(s), tonumber(l)\r\n        local hex_color = hsl_to_hex(h, s, l)\r\n        return MiniHipatterns.compute_hex_color_group(hex_color, 'bg')\r\n      end,\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Basically, this boils down to programming two parts:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1fdbb864e2015eb6f501394d593630f825154385/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L149-L161\">Pattern to be highlighted</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1fdbb864e2015eb6f501394d593630f825154385/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L163-L174\">Group used to highlight pattern matches</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In case of HSL the real problem is to convert matched color representation in HSL to its hex string (which is the only big color space Neovim highlight groups support).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is an example of how I would do it to highlight one of the CSS formats like <code class=\"notranslate\">hsl(50 80% 40%)</code> (taken from <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/hsl\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a>):</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local hsl_to_hex = function(h, s, l)\n  -- Actually convert h, s, l numbers into hex color in '#RRGGBB' format\n  return '#111111'\nend\n\nrequire('mini.hipatterns').setup({\n  highlighters = {\n    hsl_color = {\n      pattern = 'hsl%(%d+ %d+%% %d+%%%)',\n      group = function(_, match)\n        local h, s, l = match:match('hsl%((%d+) (%d+)%% (%d+)%%%)')\n        h, s, l = tonumber(h), tonumber(s), tonumber(l)\n        local hex_color = hsl_to_hex(h, s, l)\n        return MiniHipatterns.compute_hex_color_group(hex_color, 'bg')\n      end,\n    },\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">hsl_to_hex</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">h</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">s</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">l</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Actually convert h, s, l numbers into hex color in '#RRGGBB' format</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>#111111<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.hipatterns<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">highlighters</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">hsl_color</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>hsl%(%d+ %d+%% %d+%%%)<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-en\">group</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">_</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">match</span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">h</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">s</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">l</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">match</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">match</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>hsl%((%d+) (%d+)%% (%d+)%%%)<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">h</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">s</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">l</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">tonumber</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">h</span>), <span class=\"pl-c1\">tonumber</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">s</span>), <span class=\"pl-c1\">tonumber</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">l</span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">hex_color</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">hsl_to_hex</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">h</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">s</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">l</span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniHipatterns</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">compute_hex_color_group</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">hex_color</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>bg<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n      <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n    },\n  },\n})</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "Basically, this boils down to programming two parts:\n\nPattern to be highlighted.\nGroup used to highlight pattern matches.\n\nIn case of HSL the real problem is to convert matched color representation in HSL to its hex string (which is the only big color space Neovim highlight groups support).\nHere is an example of how I would do it to highlight one of the CSS formats like hsl(50 80% 40%) (taken from here):\nlocal hsl_to_hex = function(h, s, l)\n  -- Actually convert h, s, l numbers into hex color in '#RRGGBB' format\n  return '#111111'\nend\n\nrequire('mini.hipatterns').setup({\n  highlighters = {\n    hsl_color = {\n      pattern = 'hsl%(%d+ %d+%% %d+%%%)',\n      group = function(_, match)\n        local h, s, l = match:match('hsl%((%d+) (%d+)%% (%d+)%%%)')\n        h, s, l = tonumber(h), tonumber(s), tonumber(l)\n        local hex_color = hsl_to_hex(h, s, l)\n        return MiniHipatterns.compute_hex_color_group(hex_color, 'bg')\n      end,\n    },\n  },\n})",
